    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing the clear anchor for the lineup; his score of 84.28 is bolstered by a favorable 4.41 xERA matchup against Taillon and an elite 0.421 xwOBA that signals prime production potential. Alongside him, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is an essential start despite hitting in the bottom third of the order. His massive 82.13 score is driven by a juicy 4.97 xERA matchup and, crucially, his elite sprint speed against a slow-delivery pitcher, making him a primary target for stolen base opportunities\u2014our scarcest category. Meanwhile, **Dillon Dingler**, **Trea Turner**, and **Kyle Schwarber** all clear the 60.0 threshold, with **Dillon Dingler** benefiting from a significant 14% platoon boost that elevates him into a must-start status.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was the exclusion of **Chase Meidroth**, who finished with a 37.18 score. While his base projection remained respectable, a 19% penalty due to the skill of the opposing pitcher and a failure to break the 40.0 \"Zebras Floor\" left him as the odd man out in favor of higher-ceiling options. We are also proceeding with caution regarding **Junior Caminero**; while he is currently active in the utility slot, his score of 58.40 is heavily suppressed by a 0.00 xERA matchup against the ace-level arm of Cole, effectively neutralizing his platoon advantage. Managers should monitor weather closely, but the primary risk remains the high-skill profiles of pitchers like Cole and Henderson, which have tempered the expectations for **Junior Caminero** and **Hyeseong Kim** respectively. Elsewhere, we continue to stash **Zac Veen** and **Lars Nootbaar** while waiting for their return to the active roster, ensuring no game caps are wasted on non-contributors like **Colt Keith** while he remains outside the starting nine.",
